  "dct_description_sm": [
    "<span style='color:rgb(77, 77, 77);'>Underground enclosure is a general-purpose class that’s </span><span style='color:rgb(77, 77, 77);'>intended to house various types of aspatial </span><span style='color:rgb(77, 77, 77);'>equipment found in a water system. The </span><span style='color:rgb(77, 77, 77);'>underground enclosures allow access to and provide </span><span style='color:rgb(77, 77, 77);'>protection of facilities and equipment in the water </span><span style='color:rgb(77, 77, 77);'>system. The contained equipment does not </span><span style='color:rgb(77, 77, 77);'>participate in the network—their relationship to </span><span style='color:rgb(77, 77, 77);'>the underground equipment is via peer-to-peer </span><span style='color:rgb(77, 77, 77);'>associations. The types of underground enclosures </span><span style='color:rgb(77, 77, 77);'>are meter box, valve vault, and vault.</span>"
  ],
